			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2241311">
									

<p>I find myself asking what unauthorized D-class were doing in the (presumably monitored or at least locked) enclosure in the first place, let alone during 'restricted hours.'</p>
<p>Locking the doors to the enclosure between 8:55 p.m. and 6:05 a.m would prevent this kind of thing from happening again, and would cost nothing to implement.</p>
<p>Is the implication that the D-class were somehow &quot;drawn&quot; to the enclosure? If so, this is a perfect opportunity for an Incident Report adding a touch of the human perspective.</p>
<p>Regardless, the preparer of this report should at the very least mention that having the D-class in there was unauthorized, and an investigation is under way to determine how or why they got in there.</p>

